    <statement><p>Find the gradient of the function
<m>f(x,y,z) = xy^{4}</m>, at the point <m>(-1,1,0)</m></p>
<p><m>\nabla f(-1,1,0) =</m> <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\,\mathit{\vec i}-4\,\mathit{\vec j}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f_x=y^{4}</m>,  <m>f_y=x\cdot 4y^{3}</m> and  <m>f_z =0</m>.
Thus <m>\mbox{grad} f = y^{4}\,\mathit{\vec i}+x\cdot 4y^{3}\,\mathit{\vec j}+0\,\mathit{\vec k}</m> and
<m>\nabla f(-1,1,0) = \,\mathit{\vec i}-4\,\mathit{\vec j}</m>.




</solution>
